{
  "_about": "The Haluna shopkeeper at the market stall (haluna.tscn NPCs/Town/Shopkeeper, the haluna_market shop), about 56 (M3-CHR-512). A portly, genial trader who has sold the village its rope and lamp oil for thirty years: grey cropped hair receding at the temples, a grey stubble, an indigo wrap shirt with sleeves to the mid-forearm, sand shin trousers, a sea-blue trader's apron straight over the trousers, a madder-red sash (the market's one saturated note), sandals. Reach-bands left 4, right 4 from his young years at sea. Face sliders relative to the MakeHuman donor (ADR 0021: 1.0 / 0.0 = unchanged). Keys starting with '_' are read by the villager_* modules (villager_hair, villager_costume, villager_textures, write_materials, villager_clips), not by bb_params.",
